+## Bounded color-matching teaching review
+
+For selected v4 source SHA-256
+`15eba3d46c6b9cc618fb1d229cc6581dfe2a4d373cfe93a00da8c47ea42304b9`,
+one rival pairs source objects and singleton anchors independently from left to
+right, ignoring color, then stamps each object's original color. The finite
+screen of seeds 0..7, sample indices 0..3, found no generated three-demo-fit /
+query-fail episode. This is a bounded no-finding for that generated sample.
+
+Seed 2's first three generated demonstrations do fit this rival. An explicitly
+authored, validator-lawful 8x10 query reverses the two color anchors; protected
+Racket confirms the rival matches all three demos and differs from the canonical
+rule at eight query cells. All four inputs pass `self_check`; both rules were
+executed on all four inputs (eight protected Racket calls). This demonstrates
+that those three demos alone do not require color matching. It is not a claim
+that the authored query was a default draw, an estimated population failure
+rate, or a production-rule error.
+
+Reusable probe: `workspace/learnability_probe.py`. Exact programs, source/probe
+hashes, inputs, labels, runtime identity, finite screening masks, and replay
+command: `checks/419ed66194f2/learnability-witness.json` in the review return.
+The proposed teaching improvement is to include at least one permuted layout
+among each lesson's demonstrations. This remains an unimplemented proposal;
+production source, reference rule, and approval/disposition records are unchanged.
